<BaseLayout title="Exhaust" description="Headers, heat, and exhaust notes for LS Genesis Coupe swaps.">
  <h1>Exhaust</h1>
  <p>
    Header choice is tied to engine mounts and steering/rack clearance. Long-tubes, mid-lengths, and turbo manifolds are all in use depending on goals.
  </p>

  <h2>Heat Management</h2>
  <p>
    Without tunnel shielding and exhaust wrap or coatings, cabin heat (especially at the gas pedal) becomes a real problem.
    Budget for DEI-style tunnel shielding in addition to whatever you do on the pipes themselves.
  </p>

  <h2>Cats &amp; Legal</h2>
  <p>
    Emissions legality depends on your state. Plan catalytic converters and O2 sensor locations if you need to stay compliant or pass inspection.
  </p>

  <h2>Sound &amp; Routing</h2>
  <p>
    Dual exhaust exits and axle-back choices are wide open once the mid-pipes clear the tunnel and crossmember.
    Dry-fit before final welding — LS swaps change the underbody packaging versus the stock 2.0T or 3.8.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
